    "review": "# Blind admission review\n\nI found no ambiguity or inconsistency requiring a wording change. I read only the public brief, starter, and public tests. The public assertions cover an empty index, cross-channel isolation, and an older publication that follows a withdrawal in input order. They leave reinstatement, equal revisions, and build zero unillustrated. The brief determines the expected result for each.\n\nI interpreted revision order independently for each build in the requested channel. Equal revisions can retain either row because their states agree. After resolving every build, I choose the highest published one, including zero. A withdrawal of the highest build can expose a lower published build. When every build is withdrawn or the channel is absent, the result is null.\n\nMy first submission is in `current-release.cjs`. It scans the records once, retains references to the latest records in a map keyed by build, and scans that map once. It only reads the caller's records. I did not execute the submission or receive evaluator feedback.\n\n**Human engineer estimate** Roughly 3\u20137 minutes for an engineer familiar with JavaScript to read the brief, implement the two scans, run the public tests in a ready environment, and check the boundary cases. This is a judgment for one small task. Familiarity with Map and time spent adding examples could move it outside that range.\n\n**Measured blind attempt wall time** 27 seconds, from 2026-11-18 19:55:29 to 2026-11-18 19:55:56 UTC. The interval covers public input discovery, reading, interpretation, and writing the first solution and review.\n",
